%% Fee conservation Σ⟦c⟧ → F_v → Σ⟦v⟧ (F-C/F-D). For each admitted client deploy a
%% FLAT one-token FeeExtract is carved from the client's supply pool Σ⟦c⟧ into the
%% validator fee pool F_v (a conserving transfer: client debited == F_v credited,
%% never a mint); at the epoch boundary F_v is converted 1:1, backed by the carve,
%% into the validator pool Σ⟦v⟧. The Sankey is balanced left-to-right (Σ in = Σ out)
%% = the conservation theorem fee_collect_then_convert_conserves. (Three clients as
%% a representative example; the flat fee is one token per admitted deploy
%% regardless of arity. ASCII labels — mermaid sankey-beta cannot tokenize Unicode;
%% the Σ⟦·⟧ reading is in the prose.)
%% Source of truth: cost-accounting-spec-alignment-audit.md (F-C/F-D fee path).
%% Render: mmdc -i fee-conservation-sankey.mmd -o fee-conservation-sankey.svg
sankey-beta

